
=== A  Handbook material values (stated here) against the page's values ===
Handbook values used for comparison:
  copper: IACS 100 % = 1/(1.7241e-8 ohm m) = 5.800e7 S/m; pure annealed Cu at 20 C 5.96e7 S/m (CRC rho = 1.678e-8)
  aluminium: pure Al at 20 C rho = 2.65e-8 ohm m -> 3.77e7 S/m (CRC); EC grade (61 % IACS) 3.54e7; Rao Table 5.1: 3.5e7
  seawater: 4.29 S/m at S = 35, 15 C (PSS-78 reference C(35,15,0) = 42.914 mS/cm); 3-6 S/m over 0-30 C;
            static eps_r about 70-81 (pure water 80.1 at 20 C; salt lowers it; ITU-R P.368 uses 70 for sea water)
  fresh water: 1e-4 .. 1e-2 S/m (ITU-R P.368 'fresh water' 3e-3 S/m, eps_r 80); eps_r 80.1 at 20 C
  loam / moist soil: ITU-R P.527-6 sec. 4.1 'normally on the order of 1e-2 S/m', 'as low as 1e-4 S/m' dried;
            eps_r of wet soils 10-30 (Rao 'wet earth' 10; ITU-R P.368 'wet ground' 30)
  dry earth: Rao 1e-5 S/m, eps_r 5; ITU-R P.368 'very dry ground' 1e-4 S/m, eps_r 3
  Bakelite (phenolic): volume resistivity 1e9..1e12 ohm m -> 1e-12..1e-9 S/m; eps_r 4.4-7 (Rao 4.9)
  mica (muscovite): volume resistivity 1e11..1e15 ohm m; eps_r 5.4-8.7 (Rao 6)
  copper Drude collision rate nu = N e^2/(m sigma) with N = 8.47e28 m^-3
